[ti:Danny Boy]
[ar:Fred Weatherly (1913)]
[length:03:38]
[by:SingLearn - Nhom 10 (auto-aligned, faster-whisper)]
[00:00.00]Oh Danny boy, the pipes, the pipes are calling,
[00:11.94]From glen to glen, and down the mountain side.
[00:22.78]The summer's gone, and all the roses falling,
[00:34.86]'Tis you, 'tis you must go and I must bide.
[00:45.60]But come ye back when summer's in the meadow,
[00:57.14]Or when the valley's hushed and white with snow,
[01:10.02]'Tis I'll be here in sunshine or in shadow,
[01:27.46]Oh Danny boy, oh Danny boy, I love you so.
[02:12.74]But if ye come, and all the flowers are dying,
[02:19.88]If I am dead, as dead I well may be,
[02:29.24]Ye'll come and find the place where I am lying,
[02:39.02]And kneel and say an Ave there for me.
[02:48.56]And I shall hear, though soft you tread above me,
[02:58.18]And all my grave will warm and sweeter be,
[03:07.70]For you will bend and tell me that you love me,
[03:18.96]And I shall sleep in peace until you come to me.
[03:31.34]
